          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.4.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-10-06\nTHE SHELL, as the code has it since 2026-10-04 (UI-67, UI-72, UI-74 to UI-76): over the 3D, top left, looking (the camera as one menu and Cerrado · Abierto · Armado as icons); top right, «Editar: Exterior · Interior» (icons only on a phone); the measures switch alone at the bottom right. The panel has two tabs, Conversación and Materiales: the Mueble tab is gone and the furniture is edited in a mode entered from the scene. The header's second line ends with where the design comes from (the ficha's code and version, or «Personalizado»). Pencil has no door-open icon, so «Abierto» is drawn with a door.\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110–#117, #123–#128, #135, #137–#138, #142–#147): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text, amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory above the conversation (UI-4), a quiet \"+\" (UI-11), the cost first in Materials (UI-16), History and Notices without nested cards, the tray on one line, the usage-review proposals (#135), edge profiles and the focus chip (#137, #138), and the cabinet's pulls, hinges, cuts and finish (#142–#147). Open decisions are in CODE_CHANGES §7. Icons in this file are Pencil's (no fill weight, no hammer): the code's icons win. Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe rest of the Studio's sections in the same grammar as band 1.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nTap a piece, \"Editar a mano\"; «Editar: Exterior · Interior» over the 3D; the Materiales tab; the version button and the bell in the header.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Piece / Editing by hand — the edit form lives in the piece sheet, the 3D stays whole (B-2); move buttons follow the piece's axis (PieceEditor.tsx MOVE)\n- Piece / Hidden, show all — \"Ocultar\" in the piece sheet hides it; while any piece is hidden the status chip says \"1 pieza oculta\" with \"Mostrar todo\", ahead of a proposal (decided 2026-09-28, #131)\n- History keeps \"Bitácora: qué hizo el experto\" under the list, and \"Qué cambió\" is a flat line (decided 2026-09-28)\n- Edit (captures of the app, 2026-10-06; the Furniture column they replace drew the Mueble tab, gone with UI-72 and UI-74): Outside, the parts (the kind, Tamaño, Madera y acabado, Armado, Base, Cuerpo, Puertas, Cajones, each with how it is now, and «Ahorrar material»); a part (wood and finish; the base with its joints, and the joint catalog opened from «Cambiar»); a kind change that needs a redo; nothing to save; Inside, the parts («Huecos y repisas»); a cell chosen on the furniture, with «Dividir» and «Juntar» on the scene and its options in the panel; changes not applied (the draft bar: Aplicar, Deshacer, Descartar); leaving with changes («Aplicar y salir», «Descartar», «Seguir editando»). «Terminar de editar» sits at the foot of the scene on a phone and at the top on desktop (UI-76)\n- Scene (captures): the furniture open (drawers out, doors swung) and taken apart\n- Piece / Edge profile (scroll) — the face drawing hatches the piece an edge rests against and dots the chosen edges that will not show; a ⚠ on the chip and a note for each; a ⚠ on a profile the board or the tools do not allow opens the reason (Edges.tsx, #137, #138)\n- Materials / Review gate, Knotty alone (capture): without an expert the intro says Knotty reviews the numbers and a carpenter joins with an expert connected (Verdict.tsx)\n- Materials / Fix before buying — cost first (UI-16), then the verdict and the checks; sentence-case labels (UI-2)\n- Notices / Nothing pending, Materials / Cut list and Sheet layout: captures of the app, retaken 2026-10-06\n- History / Two versions — a flat timeline, no card inside a card; \"Volver a esta\" is a visible button (UI-17 family)\n- Captures retaken 2026-10-06 on the sideboard base: cut settings, editing a price, viewing an old version, Ajustes (the providers, Claude chosen, and its Tu herramienta and Avanzado sections) and confirming \"Nuevo diseño\". STALE, still the shell of 2026-09-28 because the simulated expert cannot reach them: the expert asks with options, the expert failed with \"Reintentar\", a hand edit rejected, reviewing, not viable, and unlocking saved keys\n- Conversation / Expert's memory, open — the memory folds above the conversation: closed it is one line with a count; open it holds the requirements, the design decisions and the add-note field (UI-4, src/ui/chat/Memory.tsx)\nCaptures retaken 2026-09-28 with #131 (camera, shadows, hide) and #132 (no nested cards, flat \"Qué cambió\", suggestions give way to the tray)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nHand edits apply at once and are checked like any change; the plan applies on \"Aplicar\" (D34). The list stays behind the review (D30).\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/studio/{PieceEditor,EditPanel,OutsideList,PartsList,PartSheet,CellSheet,DraftBar,SavingSheet,Joints,Materials,Verdict,HistoryPanel}.tsx and the parts each module declares (src/domain/furniture/modules/); src/ui/chat/Memory.tsx; src/ui/studio/{PieceSheet,Studio,StatusChip}.tsx for \"Ocultar\", the hidden and focus chips; src/ui/studio/{FinishSection,FinishSelect,Edges}.tsx and src/domain/furniture/modules/cabinet.ts (CABINET_LABELS) for the finish, the edges and the cabinet's fields; verdict text from the simulated expert. \"~$3,165\" from the v2 capture.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nSeveral pieces hidden: the same chip, \"N piezas ocultas\". Edit: the other parts (Tamaño, Armado, Cuerpo, Puertas, Cajones) repeat the grammar of the two captured; a design without a ficha (\"Este mueble no tiene ficha…\" and its piece list) and a plan the expert left behind are not reachable without an expert; dragging a line between cells; ways to use fewer sheets when there are some, and their locks; the parts of a bed, a table and a shoe rack (UI-73, UI-77); a cell's own pull and fronts chosen (UI-78). Edge profile: a piece with no hidden edge has no hatched strip and no notes.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-2, UI-16, UI-17, UI-59, UI-61, UI-67 to UI-78, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.\nThe 2026-09-28 proposals (dismiss a question, suggestions wrap, what changed folded, trade terms, where to reinforce, save material with locks, joints by tool level, edge profiles) are in code (#135, #137, #138).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
