    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Kx49B",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 12356,
      "name": "BRIEF — Studio · desktop",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1320,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-2xl",
      "stroke": "$line",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "L9EAF",
          "name": "Heading",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "BRIEF — Studio · desktop",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hZMSC",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.4.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-10-06\nTHE SHELL, as the code has it since 2026-10-04 (UI-67, UI-72, UI-74 to UI-76): over the 3D, top left, looking (the camera as one menu and Cerrado · Abierto · Armado as icons); top right, «Editar: Exterior · Interior» (icons only on a phone); the measures switch alone at the bottom right. The panel has two tabs, Conversación and Materiales: the Mueble tab is gone and the furniture is edited in a mode entered from the scene. The header's second line ends with where the design comes from (the ficha's code and version, or «Personalizado»). Pencil has no door-open icon, so «Abierto» is drawn with a door.\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110–#117, #123–#128, #135, #137–#138, #142–#147): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text, amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory above the conversation (UI-4), a quiet \"+\" (UI-11), the cost first in Materials (UI-16), History and Notices without nested cards, the tray on one line, the usage-review proposals (#135), edge profiles and the focus chip (#137, #138), and the cabinet's pulls, hinges, cuts and finish (#142–#147). Open decisions are in CODE_CHANGES §7. Icons in this file are Pencil's (no fill weight, no hammer): the code's icons win. Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe same Studio at a desk (D38: equal weight): 3D on the left, a 420 px panel on the right.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nSame as the mobile bands.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Conversation / Default — with an expert connected (\"Claude · claude-opus-5\" in the header); \"Nuevo diseño\" as a ghost (UI-11, Doña Carmen); the scene bar's states and the measures switch are icons with a title. Conversation / No expert, connect (capture)\n- Piece / Selected, editing — the piece takes the panel, same pattern as mobile; editing is open because there is room (B-2); the fields carry mm only, no cm line (decided 2026-09-28); \"Ocultar\" next to the close button\n- Conversation / Proposal pending — status chip over the 3D; ⚡ fix as the primary action; \"bajo mi riesgo\" a visible secondary (UI-6, UI-17)\n- Piece / Selected, editing — the status chip \"Enfocada: <pieza>\" with \"Ver todo el mueble\" sits under the scene bar (#137)\n- Edit (captures of the app, 2026-10-06): Outside, the parts; a part (base); the joint catalog; nothing to save; Inside, the parts; a cell chosen; changes not applied; leaving with changes. Scene (captures): open and taken apart\n- Piece / Edge profile — the hatched strip, dotted hidden edges and per-edge notes, as mobile (#137, #138)\n- Materials / Review gate, Knotty alone, and Can be made (captures)\n- Notices / Several, after choosing — one \"Resolver 2\" (UI-15)\n- Notices / Nothing pending, Materials / Cut list and Sheet layout: captures of the app, retaken 2026-10-06\n- Settings (the dialog is «Ajustes»: providers, Claude chosen, Tu herramienta and Avanzado) and New design confirm: captures of the app, retaken 2026-10-06\n- Materials / Cost first, expert working — cost and sheets without waiting, the expert working in the background with the global indicator (UI-15, UI-16)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nDesktop ≥ 768 px (Studio.tsx useDesktop). D30, D34, D36, D37 unchanged.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nSame as the mobile bands, plus the sheet rows from Materials.tsx.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nHidden pieces on desktop: the same chip as mobile. The review gate's check list and the sheet diagrams stay as the app draws them (decided 2026-09-28): see the Materials captures.\nThe rest of the states on desktop are the mobile ones in the side panel; history is the same, wider; the parts and cell options not captured on desktop are the mobile ones.\nLIFT, later: the piece sheet leaves half the desktop panel empty — room for the piece's cut-list line and its joints drawn.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-6, UI-11, UI-15, UI-16, UI-17, UI-67 to UI-78, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
